=== R1b: SPIKE TEST -- proof that HC_contrast is NOT matching ===
inject a large-norm spike at a NON-matched candidate k*; a matcher must
ignore it (it is not a match), a contrast latch must jump to it.
  spike at k*= 8, tau=2 :  matcher argmin = 2 (want 2)   contrast argmin = 8 (want 8)
  spike at k*= 8, tau=3 :  matcher argmin = 3 (want 3)   contrast argmin = 8 (want 8)
  spike at k*= 9, tau=2 :  matcher argmin = 2 (want 2)   contrast argmin = 9 (want 9)
  spike at k*= 9, tau=3 :  matcher argmin = 3 (want 3)   contrast argmin = 9 (want 9)
  spike at k*=10, tau=2 :  matcher argmin = 2 (want 2)   contrast argmin = 10 (want 10)
  spike at k*=10, tau=3 :  matcher argmin = 3 (want 3)   contrast argmin = 10 (want 10)
  -> the two operators are DIFFERENT FUNCTIONS; they only agree when the
     matched slice is the only anomaly, which is exactly the synthetic case.

