============================================================================
R2  IS THE P2 FALLBACK CLAIM ALREADY TRUE AT RANDOM INITIALISATION?
============================================================================
claim under test: 'the aggregation is NOT a pointwise function of each
candidate slice' -- detected by Delta_P2 != 0 (P2 = permute, then apply
pi^-1 to the aggregated cost before readout).

random-weight aggregations: 12 seeds x 6 permutations x 6 tau = 432 units
  |Delta_P2|            : mean 0.644  median 0.461  p95 2.061
  |m_P2 - m_orig|       : mean 0.694  median 0.510  p95 2.316
  relative cost deviation max|A(Vopi)opi^-1 - A(V)| / max|A(V)|:
        mean 0.8735  median 0.7862  min 0.5306
  units with a NON-ZERO cost deviation: 432 of 432

  -> a RANDOMLY INITIALISED aggregation is already non-pointwise in k, in
     100%% of units.  The P2 claim is a property of the ARCHITECTURE, not
     of training.  It cannot separate a trained model from random weights.

============================================================================
R3  THE k-AXIS ZERO PADDING IS NOT NUISANCE-MATCHED
============================================================================
Conv3d pads k with zeros, so k=0 and k=11 are treated differently from the
interior.  A permutation changes WHICH slice sits there.

  single transposition moving the matched slice to position `dest`
  (everything else identical).  Random Conv3d aggregation, tau = 3.
  dest :  m_P1     |cost change|rel   (dest 0 and 11 are the PADDED ends)
    0  :   5.294           0.5987  <-- padded boundary
    1  :   5.394           0.5608
    2  :   5.290           0.5023
    3  :   5.252           0.0000
    4  :   5.371           0.5583
    5  :   5.397           0.7016
    6  :   5.432           0.6005
    7  :   5.282           0.5573
    8  :   5.459           0.5878
    9  :   5.232           0.6022
   10  :   5.438           0.6008
   11  :   5.274           0.5294  <-- padded boundary

  -> the size of the permutation's effect depends on WHERE the matched
     slice lands, including whether it lands against the zero padding.
     'same weights, same input' does not make the two arms exchangeable.
